{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And he blessed him and said.</b> One needs to know whether the blessing he blessed him is what is mentioned in the passage ״בָּרוּךְ אַבְרָם״ — if so, there was no need to say ״וַיְבָרְכֵהוּ״, and it appears to me from his saying ״בָּרוּךְ אַבְרָם״ that this is the blessing he gave him. <b>Further</b>, he should have said ״וַיְבָרְכֵהוּ לֵאמֹר בָּרוּךְ״ etc., in the manner of His saying (Genesis 48:20) ״וַיְבָרְכֵם בַּיּוֹם הַהוּא לֵאמֹר״ etc." "<b>However</b>, the intention is: first he blessed Abraham — meaning, a blessing pertaining to him personally, that he not fall into the hands of his enemies and that his forces be successful; these are the physical blessings. And afterward he said another matter, speaking of the supernal dimension: ״בָּרוּךְ אַבְרָם״ — and his blessing shall be to El Elyon, that he will worship the El, and that through his merit the El will be the possessor of heaven and earth. And so it was, for through Abraham's merit HaShem gave eternal life to his children and the heavens and earth were sustained, as they said, of blessed memory (Avodah Zarah 3a), that the Holy One, blessed be He, made a condition with the work of Creation, etc., and as they said (Shabbat 88a) on the verse (Psalms 76:9) ״אֶרֶץ יָרְאָה״ etc. See then that were it not for Abraham, HaShem would have no possession of heaven and earth — understand this." "<b>Further</b>, it intends along this line: <b>and he blessed him</b> etc. — to inform us that the two blessings stated in his words are both blessings pertaining to Abraham, and even the blessing he said, ״בָּרוּךְ אֵל עֶלְיוֹן אֲשֶׁר מִגֵּן״, is a blessing for Abraham — when HaShem is blessed through his merit, who is אֲשֶׁר מִגֵּן etc., and he never blessed except with the blessings stated in the passage."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:41:18.737614425Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}